# CatBoost embeds a training-run timestamp/GUID in .cbm model files, so a
# byte-for-byte identical fit produces a different file every run (predictions
# are bit-identical; only the container metadata varies -- see
# catboost-8z4.3-report.md and docs/phase-0/README.md). Committing them would
# make every fixture regeneration a spurious diff, so they are regenerated by
# tools/oracle/gen_smoke_fixture.py and tools/oracle/cli/gen_smoke_fixture.sh
# instead of tracked.
tests/fixtures/oracle/smoke_model.cbm
tests/fixtures/oracle-cli/smoke_model.cbm
.tmp-build/
# NPar::RunMaster (distributed training, catboost-8z4.103) writes a network-
# delay measurement file as a side effect into the process's cwd -- not a
# training artifact governed by allow_writing_files, and not deterministic.
tests/testthat/delay_matrix.bin
